15 via root's crontab, appending output to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log. The script file found on disk was corrupted (contained a leftover heredoc delimiter and stray shell commands as literal text instead of being executable), so it was rewritten as a clean POSIX sh script and made executable (0755, root:root) before installing the cron entry. Verified the full pipeline end-to-end, then performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured a pre-restart boot_id baseline, issued a self-acknowledging systemctl reboot, polled until exec access returned, confirmed the boot_id changed, and verified crond, the crontab entry, the executable script, and the log file all survived and functioned correctly post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS (RHEL 10.0) and existing /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance file, found it corrupted with leftover heredoc/shell text\",\"Rewrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance as a clean POSIX sh script, set ownership root:root and mode 0755\",\"Verified crond service active and enabled on node1\",\"Installed root crontab entry: '15 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance >> /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log 2>&1' and confirmed persistence in /var/spool/cron/root\",\"Created /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log with root:root ownership\",\"Ran the script manually through the exact redirection cron will use, confirmed correct log output\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, crond active state, crontab contents, log contents\",\"Issued self-acknowledging 'systemctl reboot' via backgrounded/detached shell so the exec call returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned; confirmed new boot_id and fresh uptime proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: crond active/enabled, crontab entry intact, script executable and present, log content preserved\",\"Re-ran the maintenance script post-restart to confirm continued correct functioning and log append behavior\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Script /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance exists, is a valid executable, and produces correct output\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-601de518d8014b27\",\"cmd-27671cfb9e4f4e91\",\"cmd-42ca2a4ec2b44c93\"],\"summary\":\"Discovered the original script file was corrupted (literal heredoc/shell text instead of executable code); rewrote it as a valid POSIX sh script, set 0755/root:root, and confirmed it runs and prints the expected completion line\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cron schedules the script daily at 02:15 and output is retained in /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f0927383fac9448d\",\"cmd-555a29ad149b4843\",\"cmd-0ede0352f17b439e\"],\"summary\":\"Installed root crontab line '15 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance >> /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log 2>&1', confirmed it persisted to /var/spool/cron/root, and ran it exactly as cron would to confirm output is correctly appended to the log file\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline for node1 (boot identity, cron config, service state, log data)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8f0897749af84902\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id=368725cb..., crond active, crontab entry present, and existing log content before restarting\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect (node1)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1ffc3e786bdf4334\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'systemctl reboot' with a short delay so the exec call acknowledged and returned before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 boot identity changed, proving an actual restart (not just elapsed time)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ea85778bedc445bb\",\"cmd-22213abb60c247e7\",\"cmd-56edfef4d25a4cae\"],\"summary\":\"Exec calls timed out while node1 was rebooting; once exec access returned, boot_id had changed from 368725cb-... to 1c0f7716-... with a fresh uptime timestamp, proving a genuine restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of cron job, service, and log data on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-97ea0bedd4ac41a0\",\"cmd-029772cfcb1847b7\"],\"summary\":\"After the reboot, crond was active/enabled, the crontab entry and executable script were intact, prior log content survived, and a fresh manual run appended a new correctly formatted log line\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to run /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance daily at 02:15 via root's crontab, appending output to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log. The script file found on disk was corrupted (contained a leftover heredoc delimiter and stray shell commands as literal text instead of being executable), so it was rewritten as a clean POSIX sh script and made executable (0755, root:root) before installing the cron entry. Verified the full pipeline end-to-end, then performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured a pre-restart boot_id baseline, issued a self-acknowledging systemctl reboot, polled until exec access returned, confirmed the boot_id changed, and verified crond, the crontab entry, the executable script, and the log file all survived and functioned correctly post-restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS (RHEL 10.0) and existing /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance file, found it corrupted with leftover heredoc/shell text","Rewrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance as a clean POSIX sh script, set ownership root:root and mode 0755","Verified crond service active and enabled on node1","Installed root crontab entry: '15 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance >> /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log 2>&1' and confirmed persistence in /var/spool/cron/root","Created /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log with root:root ownership","Ran the script manually through the exact redirection cron will use, confirmed correct log output","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, crond active state, crontab contents, log contents","Issued self-acknowledging 'systemctl reboot' via backgrounded/detached shell so the exec call returned 